{
 "summary": "Checkout failures are a timeout cascade that most likely originates in inventory POST /reserve, which slowed right after inventory was deployed 3.1.5 -> 3.2.1 at 07:18:17Z. Inventory returns no 5xx but its p95 latency rose to 4.77s. Orders times out with 504s from 07:18:32Z, reaching 100% errors, and gateway returns 502s from 07:18:47Z, peaking at 71.8%. Rolling back inventory to 3.1.5 is the leading mitigation; logs could not be queried.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "The inventory 3.2.1 deploy most likely introduced a latency regression in POST /reserve. Every sampled failing trace spends most of its self time there (about 2.4-2.6s, release 3.2.1). Orders then times out (504) and gateway returns 502. The connection to the deploy rests on timing and on the traces running 3.2.1; no logs or diff confirm the specific change.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-190058c637be",
   "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
   "ev-51525d7035d0",
   "ev-1da116a62fee",
   "ev-c000e6b4f684"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders appears to have a timeout shorter than inventory's degraded latency, so it returns 504 instead of waiting. Its error ratio hit 100% while inventory itself served 0% 5xx.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-1da116a62fee",
    "ev-51525d7035d0",
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Gateway turns the orders 504s into 502s on POST /checkout, which is where users see the failures.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:17Z",
   "event": "inventory deployed 3.1.5 -> 3.2.1 by ci-pipeline",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-190058c637be"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:32Z",
   "event": "orders 5xx ratio and p95 latency cross their thresholds (5% errors, 1s latency)",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-1da116a62fee"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:47Z",
   "event": "inventory p95 latency crosses 1s; gateway 5xx ratio and p95 latency cross their thresholds",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-51525d7035d0",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:20:33Z",
   "event": "Sampled error traces show gateway 502 <- orders 504, with dominant self time in inventory POST /reserve (3.2.1)",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders or gateway as the origin is unlikely: trace self time is concentrated in inventory POST /reserve, and those services are only reporting errors propagated from downstream.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "A traffic surge is unlikely: request rates stayed modest, about 2.1 req/s at gateway and 1.4 req/s at orders and inventory.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-c000e6b4f684",
    "ev-51525d7035d0",
    "ev-1da116a62fee"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "Logs could not be queried (backend timed out), so no inventory error messages, stack traces or timeout logs are available to confirm what in 3.2.1 is slow.",
  "It is unknown whether inventory was already slow before the deploy. The orders onset at 07:18:32Z precedes inventory's p95 threshold crossing at 07:18:47Z, likely because of 15s metric step granularity.",
  "The specific code or config change in inventory 3.2.1 is unknown, as is whether a downstream dependency of inventory (for example a database) is involved; no evidence covers inventory's dependencies.",
  "Traces were only sampled between 07:20:33Z and 07:20:43Z; there are no trace samples from the onset period."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Roll back inventory to 3.1.5.",
   "rationale": "The latency regression began right after the 3.2.1 deploy, and all sampled failing traces point to inventory 3.2.1 POST /reserve as the slow span.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-190058c637be",
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "After the rollback, confirm recovery by watching inventory p95 latency and the orders and gateway 5xx ratios.",
   "rationale": "If the errors persist after rollback, the deploy hypothesis is wrong and another cause must be investigated.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-51525d7035d0",
    "ev-1da116a62fee",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  },
